# The generated native context files (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md) must byte-match a
# fresh render of `.zirv/context/*.md`, so both sides have to be byte-stable
# across platforms:
#
# - `/.zirv/context/*.md text eol=lf` pins the render inputs to LF on every
#   checkout, regardless of core.autocrlf.
# - `/CLAUDE.md -text` / `/AGENTS.md -text` freeze the committed render output
#   exactly as generated (no normalization on either add or checkout).
#
# Patterns are anchored to the repo root: an unanchored `CLAUDE.md` matches at
# any depth, and on case-insensitive filesystems it even captures
# `.zirv/context/claude.md`.
/CLAUDE.md -text
/AGENTS.md -text
/.zirv/context/*.md text eol=lf

# The image build runs shell from these files, so a Windows checkout must not
# give them CRLF line endings.
/Dockerfile text eol=lf
/.dockerignore text eol=lf
/docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
